# Drizzle / migrations

- Schema source of truth is the project's Drizzle schema directory.
- Generate migrations with the repository's existing DB script.
- Review generated SQL before applying it.
- Never silently rewrite an already-applied migration.
- Prefer safe/idempotent SQL when repairing development databases.
- Never use destructive repair/reset commands against production.
- Preserve foreign-key and uniqueness constraints.
- Add indexes for high-volume access paths.

## Important indexes

Likely high-volume indexes include:
- conversation participants by user_id
- messages by conversation_id + created_at
- unread messages/read state
- discovery profile language relationships
- blocks by blocker_id + blocked_id
- reports by status/created_at
- device tokens by user_id
- presence by user_id

Choose indexes from actual query patterns; do not add every conceivable index.

## Data integrity

Use database constraints for invariants that must never be violated.

Examples:
- one participant row per user/conversation
- one block relationship per user pair
- unique language preference relationships
- unique device token when appropriate

Use transactions when one user action changes multiple related records.
